@startuml
!theme plain
title TASK-260715-30lv40 — M1/M2/M3/app authority boundaries
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Apple system" {
  [NETunnelProviderSession.status] as SystemState
}

package "Packet-tunnel extension" {
  package "M1 authority" {
    [TunnelProviderAdapter] as Adapter
    [TunnelRuntimeCoordinator] as Coordinator
    [Packet + TCP + safe DNS + settings] as Base
    [Immutable snapshot store] as Store
  }

  package "M2 authority" {
    [Relay bootstrap/session validator] as Relay
    [Association generation] as Associations
    [Relay-only reprobe] as Reprobe
  }

  package "M3 authority" {
    [Path/host/route/lane reconnect] as Reconnect
    [Provider reasserting] as Reasserting
  }
}

package "Containing app / M4" {
  [Presentation model] as UI
}

SystemState --> UI : system session fact
Adapter --> Coordinator : runtime generation + lifecycle
Coordinator <--> Base : base control / facts
Coordinator --> Store : sole snapshot writer
Coordinator <--> Relay : relay control / facts
Relay --> Associations : owns active relay generation
Relay --> Reprobe : finite eligible reason only
Reconnect --> Coordinator : current transport generation + recovery fact
Reconnect --> Reasserting : sole writer
Reconnect --> Relay : one local validation-start event\nafter current BaseReady per transport attempt
Reconnect --> Reprobe : cancel before M3 retry
Store --> UI : versioned immutable provider truth

note bottom of UI
Combines system status and current provider snapshot for display.
Never owns runtime truth, generations, or retry loops.
end note

note bottom of Reprobe
No path resolution, host reconnect, route replacement,
lane-pool repair, sleep/wake, NAT64, or captive handling.
end note

note bottom of Relay
M2 owns candidate validation and active relay promotion.
Candidate proof is internal; M3 owns reconnect cadence.
end note

note bottom of Store
No credentials, destinations, DNS queries, payloads,
host identifiers, remote strings, or raw spawn logs.
end note
@enduml
